Put licensed BGMI artwork here (key art, character art, map imagery).

The BGMI game card currently uses an ORIGINAL cinematic scene drawn in
SVG inside index.html — night ridgelines, a transport plane on its drop
run, parachutes, a rim-lit trooper silhouette and a tactical HUD. It is
built to read as a BGMI tournament card without using any game IP,
because real BGMI key art is licensed and must not be scraped.

To swap in licensed art once you have it:

  1. Drop the image here, e.g. assets/bgmi/key-art.jpg
  2. In css/style.css, set the card's art variable:

       .game-card--bgmi {
         --card-art: url("../assets/bgmi/key-art.jpg");
         --card-art-opacity: 0.6;   /* optional, defaults to 0.5 */
       }

The image renders in .game-card__photo, which sits ABOVE the background
atmosphere and BELOW the readability gradient — so the white card text
stays legible on top of it. You can keep or remove the SVG scene: to
remove it, delete the <svg class="game-card__art"> block from the BGMI
card in index.html.
